</targetDirectedRelationshipPropertyPath_>
<text>
<val>when a limit binds the arbiter shall clamp the pump command without switching the controlled variable</val>
</text>
</SysML:Requirement>
<SysML:Requirement id="7215fed2-8e8e-11f1-926f-01c58a30f183">
<clientDependency>
<reflist>
<ref refid="724a1a00-8e8e-11f1-9802-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</clientDependency>
<externalId>
<val>REQ-SUB-ARB-005</val>
</externalId>
<name>
<val>REQ-SUB-ARB-005</val>
</name>
<owningPackage>
<ref refid="7215ec87-8e8e-11f1-9bf4-01c58a30f183"/>
</owningPackage>
<package>
<ref refid="7215ec87-8e8e-11f1-9bf4-01c58a30f183"/>
</package>
<presentation>
<reflist>
<ref refid="721cbf5d-8e8e-11f1-8a41-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</presentation>
<supplierDependency>
<reflist>
<ref refid="770d9f62-8e8e-11f1-9ecc-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</supplierDependency>
<targetDirectedRelationshipPropertyPath_>
<reflist>
<ref refid="770d9f62-8e8e-11f1-9ecc-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</targetDirectedRelationshipPropertyPath_>
<text>
<val>the active loop's integrator shall be back-calculated from the command actually applied, so entering and leaving a clamp produces no step</val>
</text>
</SysML:Requirement>
<SysML:Requirement id="72160123-8e8e-11f1-8ff2-01c58a30f183">
<clientDependency>
<reflist>
<ref refid="724a4bad-8e8e-11f1-9f8d-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</clientDependency>
<externalId>
<val>REQ-SUB-ARB-006</val>
</externalId>
<name>
<val>REQ-SUB-ARB-006</val>
</name>
<owningPackage>
<ref refid="7215ec87-8e8e-11f1-9bf4-01c58a30f183"/>
</owningPackage>
<package>
<ref refid="7215ec87-8e8e-11f1-9bf4-01c58a30f183"/>
</package>
<presentation>
<reflist>
<ref refid="721e81a4-8e8e-11f1-b669-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</presentation>
<supplierDependency>
<reflist>
<ref refid="770da374-8e8e-11f1-9b80-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</supplierDependency>
<targetDirectedRelationshipPropertyPath_>
<reflist>
<ref refid="770da374-8e8e-11f1-9b80-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</targetDirectedRelationshipPropertyPath_>
<text>
<val>on loop handover the incoming loop's integrator shall be preset so its output equals the command currently applied</val>
</text>
</SysML:Requirement>
<SysML:Requirement id="721603d9-8e8e-11f1-ab6c-01c58a30f183">
<clientDependency>
<reflist>
<ref refid="724a74f2-8e8e-11f1-be41-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</clientDependency>
<externalId>
<val>REQ-SUB-ARB-007</val>
</externalId>
<name>
<val>REQ-SUB-ARB-007</val>
</name>
<owningPackage>
<ref refid="7215ec87-8e8e-11f1-9bf4-01c58a30f183"/>
</owningPackage>
<package>
<ref refid="7215ec87-8e8e-11f1-9bf4-01c58a30f183"/>
</package>
<presentation>
<reflist>
<ref refid="7220219e-8e8e-11f1-beec-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</presentation>
<supplierDependency>
<reflist>
<ref refid="770da6d2-8e8e-11f1-8996-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</supplierDependency>
<targetDirectedRelationshipPropertyPath_>
<reflist>
<ref refid="770da6d2-8e8e-11f1-8996-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</targetDirectedRelationshipPropertyPath_>
<text>
<val>both loops shall expose an integrator preset input for use by REQ-SUB-ARB-005 and -006</val>
</text>
</SysML:Requirement>
<SysML:Requirement id="72160641-8e8e-11f1-801a-01c58a30f183">
<clientDependency>
<reflist>
<ref refid="724c4d90-8e8e-11f1-9e6c-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</clientDependency>
<externalId>
<val>REQ-SUB-ARB-008</val>
</externalId>
<name>
<val>REQ-SUB-ARB-008</val>
</name>
<owningPackage>
<ref refid="7215ec87-8e8e-11f1-9bf4-01c58a30f183"/>
</owningPackage>
<package>
<ref refid="7215ec87-8e8e-11f1-9bf4-01c58a30f183"/>
</package>
<presentation>
<reflist>
<ref refid="7230bfd6-8e8e-11f1-b72c-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</presentation>
<supplierDependency>
<reflist>
<ref refid="770daaa1-8e8e-11f1-9ed8-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</supplierDependency>
<targetDirectedRelationshipPropertyPath_>
<reflist>
<ref refid="770daaa1-8e8e-11f1-9ed8-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</targetDirectedRelationshipPropertyPath_>
<text>
<val>the arbiter shall report limit-active state for logging alongside setpoint and measured value</val>
</text>
</SysML:Requirement>
<SysML:Requirement id="7216086b-8e8e-11f1-9df6-01c58a30f183">
<clientDependency>
<reflist>
<ref refid="724fabdf-8e8e-11f1-8787-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</clientDependency>
<externalId>
<val>REQ-SUB-ARB-010</val>
</externalId>
<name>
<val>REQ-SUB-ARB-010</val>
</name>
<owningPackage>
<ref refid="7215ec87-8e8e-11f1-9bf4-01c58a30f183"/>
</owningPackage>
<package>
<ref refid="7215ec87-8e8e-11f1-9bf4-01c58a30f183"/>
</package>
<presentation>
<reflist>
<ref refid="72326455-8e8e-11f1-a5ee-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</presentation>
<supplierDependency>
<reflist>
<ref refid="770dae68-8e8e-11f1-8f88-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</supplierDependency>
<targetDirectedRelationshipPropertyPath_>
<reflist>
<ref refid="770dae68-8e8e-11f1-8f88-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</targetDirectedRelationshipPropertyPath_>
<text>
<val>the arbiter shall refuse to enable a flow loop whose setpoint lies below the measurable threshold OB-27</val>
</text>
</SysML:Requirement>
<SysML:Requirement id="72160a9f-8e8e-11f1-9df8-01c58a30f183">
<clientDependency>
<reflist>
<ref refid="725300fc-8e8e-11f1-94f0-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</clientDependency>
<externalId>
<val>REQ-SUB-ARB-011</val>
</externalId>
<name>
<val>REQ-SUB-ARB-011</val>
</name>
<owningPackage>
<ref refid="7215ec87-8e8e-11f1-9bf4-01c58a30f183"/>
</owningPackage>
<package>
<ref refid="7215ec87-8e8e-11f1-9bf4-01c58a30f183"/>
</package>
<presentation>
<reflist>
<ref refid="7234272a-8e8e-11f1-ab23-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</presentation>
<supplierDependency>
<reflist>
<ref refid="770db1ca-8e8e-11f1-b3c4-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</supplierDependency>
<targetDirectedRelationshipPropertyPath_>
<reflist>
<ref refid="770db1ca-8e8e-11f1-b3c4-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</targetDirectedRelationshipPropertyPath_>
<text>
<val>the arbiter shall abort the shot when the sensor of the controlled variable becomes invalid</val>
</text>
</SysML:Requirement>
<SysML:Requirement id="72160d24-8e8e-11f1-a3d6-01c58a30f183">
<clientDependency>
<reflist>
<ref refid="7254a08c-8e8e-11f1-98f2-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</clientDependency>
<externalId>
<val>REQ-SUB-ARB-012</val>
</externalId>
<name>
<val>REQ-SUB-ARB-012</val>
</name>
<owningPackage>
<ref refid="7215ec87-8e8e-11f1-9bf4-01c58a30f183"/>
</owningPackage>
<package>
<ref refid="7215ec87-8e8e-11f1-9bf4-01c58a30f183"/>
</package>
<presentation>
<reflist>
<ref refid="7235d44d-8e8e-11f1-bd61-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</presentation>
<supplierDependency>
<reflist>
<ref refid="770db6cb-8e8e-11f1-93cc-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</supplierDependency>
<targetDirectedRelationshipPropertyPath_>
<reflist>
<ref refid="770db6cb-8e8e-11f1-93cc-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</targetDirectedRelationshipPropertyPath_>
<text>
<val>a sensor reading that has not changed for OB-26 shall be treated as invalid</val>
</text>
</SysML:Requirement>
<SysML:Requirement id="721610f7-8e8e-11f1-84b7-01c58a30f183">
<clientDependency>
<reflist>
<ref refid="7254dde9-8e8e-11f1-84ad-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</clientDependency>
<externalId>
<val>REQ-SUB-ARB-013</val>
</externalId>
<name>
<val>REQ-SUB-ARB-013</val>
</name>
<owningPackage>
<ref refid="7215ec87-8e8e-11f1-9bf4-01c58a30f183"/>
</owningPackage>
<package>
<ref refid="7215ec87-8e8e-11f1-9bf4-01c58a30f183"/>
</package>
<presentation>
<reflist>
<ref refid="7237b590-8e8e-11f1-a735-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</presentation>
<supplierDependency>
<reflist>
<ref refid="770dbb51-8e8e-11f1-a413-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</supplierDependency>
<targetDirectedRelationshipPropertyPath_>
<reflist>
<ref refid="770dbb51-8e8e-11f1-a413-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</targetDirectedRelationshipPropertyPath_>
<text>
<val>setpoint, mode tag and limits shall be accepted as one atomic update</val>
</text>
</SysML:Requirement>
<SysML:Requirement id="7216136c-8e8e-11f1-9fd7-01c58a30f183">
<clientDependency>
<reflist>
<ref refid="72550263-8e8e-11f1-8060-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</clientDependency>
<externalId>
<val>REQ-SUB-ARB-014</val>
</externalId>
<name>
<val>REQ-SUB-ARB-014</val>
</name>
<owningPackage>
<ref refid="7215ec87-8e8e-11f1-9bf4-01c58a30f183"/>
</owningPackage>
<package>
<ref refid="7215ec87-8e8e-11f1-9bf4-01c58a30f183"/>
</package>
<presentation>
<reflist>
<ref refid="723980e1-8e8e-11f1-b700-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</presentation>
<supplierDependency>
<reflist>
<ref refid="770dbef2-8e8e-11f1-a84a-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</supplierDependency>
<targetDirectedRelationshipPropertyPath_>
<reflist>
<ref refid="770dbef2-8e8e-11f1-a84a-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</targetDirectedRelationshipPropertyPath_>
<text>
<val>a missing setpoint update shall drive the pump command to zero rather than hold the last value</val>
</text>
</SysML:Requirement>
<SysML:Requirement id="72161641-8e8e-11f1-9560-01c58a30f183">
<clientDependency>
<reflist>
<ref refid="7256f341-8e8e-11f1-8f0e-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</clientDependency>
<externalId>
<val>REQ-SUB-ARB-020</val>
</externalId>
<name>
<val>REQ-SUB-ARB-020</val>
</name>
<owningPackage>
<ref refid="7215ec87-8e8e-11f1-9bf4-01c58a30f183"/>
</owningPackage>
<package>
<ref refid="7215ec87-8e8e-11f1-9bf4-01c58a30f183"/>
</package>
<presentation>
<reflist>
<ref refid="723b865d-8e8e-11f1-8195-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</presentation>
<supplierDependency>
<reflist>
<ref refid="770dc532-8e8e-11f1-bead-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</supplierDependency>
<targetDirectedRelationshipPropertyPath_>
<reflist>
<ref refid="770dc532-8e8e-11f1-bead-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</targetDirectedRelationshipPropertyPath_>
<text>
<val>the arbiter shall saturate the pump command to the range covered by the calibrated pump map</val>
</text>
</SysML:Requirement>
<SysML:Requirement id="721618e1-8e8e-11f1-8b24-01c58a30f183">
<clientDependency>
<reflist>
<ref refid="7269728a-8e8e-11f1-ad46-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</clientDependency>
<externalId>
<val>REQ-SUB-ARB-021</val>
</externalId>
<name>
<val>REQ-SUB-ARB-021</val>
</name>
<owningPackage>
<ref refid="7215ec87-8e8e-11f1-9bf4-01c58a30f183"/>
</owningPackage>
<package>
<ref refid="7215ec87-8e8e-11f1-9bf4-01c58a30f183"/>
</package>
<presentation>
<reflist>
<ref refid="723d568d-8e8e-11f1-9b65-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</presentation>
<supplierDependency>
<reflist>
<ref refid="770dc8b6-8e8e-11f1-a18d-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</supplierDependency>
<targetDirectedRelationshipPropertyPath_>
<reflist>
<ref refid="770dc8b6-8e8e-11f1-a18d-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</targetDirectedRelationshipPropertyPath_>
<text>
<val>the safety supervisor veto shall reach the actuator without passing through the arbiter or any loop</val>
</text>
</SysML:Requirement>
<SysML:RequirementDiagram id="72161bc8-8e8e-11f1-8be8-01c58a30f183">
