</clientDependency>
<externalId>
<val>REQ-SUB-SUP-011</val>
</externalId>
<name>
<val>REQ-SUB-SUP-011</val>
</name>
<owningPackage>
<ref refid="73d002fa-8e8e-11f1-96db-01c58a30f183"/>
</owningPackage>
<package>
<ref refid="73d002fa-8e8e-11f1-96db-01c58a30f183"/>
</package>
<presentation>
<reflist>
<ref refid="73e8d60d-8e8e-11f1-9a50-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</presentation>
<supplierDependency>
<reflist>
<ref refid="770e5fe7-8e8e-11f1-a87d-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</supplierDependency>
<targetDirectedRelationshipPropertyPath_>
<reflist>
<ref refid="770e5fe7-8e8e-11f1-a87d-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</targetDirectedRelationshipPropertyPath_>
<text>
<val>publish that estimate to the thermal power cap, so loss of flow reduces heater power continuously rather than tripping a fault</val>
</text>
</SysML:Requirement>
<SysML:Requirement id="73d0184a-8e8e-11f1-84f0-01c58a30f183">
<clientDependency>
<reflist>
<ref refid="74057033-8e8e-11f1-9e39-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</clientDependency>
<externalId>
<val>REQ-SUB-SUP-012</val>
</externalId>
<name>
<val>REQ-SUB-SUP-012</val>
</name>
<owningPackage>
<ref refid="73d002fa-8e8e-11f1-96db-01c58a30f183"/>
</owningPackage>
<package>
<ref refid="73d002fa-8e8e-11f1-96db-01c58a30f183"/>
</package>
<presentation>
<reflist>
<ref refid="73eaa4a6-8e8e-11f1-b084-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</presentation>
<supplierDependency>
<reflist>
<ref refid="770e639d-8e8e-11f1-abb2-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</supplierDependency>
<targetDirectedRelationshipPropertyPath_>
<reflist>
<ref refid="770e639d-8e8e-11f1-abb2-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</targetDirectedRelationshipPropertyPath_>
<text>
<val>the decay shall be scaled to commanded flow, so a legitimate low-flow phase is not mistaken for loss of flow</val>
</text>
</SysML:Requirement>
<SysML:Requirement id="73d01c41-8e8e-11f1-9469-01c58a30f183">
<clientDependency>
<reflist>
<ref refid="74075491-8e8e-11f1-ac42-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</clientDependency>
<externalId>
<val>REQ-SUB-SUP-020</val>
</externalId>
<name>
<val>REQ-SUB-SUP-020</val>
</name>
<owningPackage>
<ref refid="73d002fa-8e8e-11f1-96db-01c58a30f183"/>
</owningPackage>
<package>
<ref refid="73d002fa-8e8e-11f1-96db-01c58a30f183"/>
</package>
<presentation>
<reflist>
<ref refid="73ec49f9-8e8e-11f1-a543-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</presentation>
<supplierDependency>
<reflist>
<ref refid="770e6720-8e8e-11f1-8d50-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</supplierDependency>
<targetDirectedRelationshipPropertyPath_>
<reflist>
<ref refid="770e6720-8e8e-11f1-8d50-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</targetDirectedRelationshipPropertyPath_>
<text>
<val>classify tank empty as a shot abort that returns to Ready, subject to the refill inhibit of REQ-SYS-066</val>
</text>
</SysML:Requirement>
<SysML:Requirement id="73d01ed9-8e8e-11f1-a0e3-01c58a30f183">
<clientDependency>
<reflist>
<ref refid="740ac3b0-8e8e-11f1-8685-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</clientDependency>
<externalId>
<val>REQ-SUB-SUP-021</val>
</externalId>
<name>
<val>REQ-SUB-SUP-021</val>
</name>
<owningPackage>
<ref refid="73d002fa-8e8e-11f1-96db-01c58a30f183"/>
</owningPackage>
<package>
<ref refid="73d002fa-8e8e-11f1-96db-01c58a30f183"/>
</package>
<presentation>
<reflist>
<ref refid="73ee1fd1-8e8e-11f1-9e17-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</presentation>
<supplierDependency>
<reflist>
<ref refid="770e6ad8-8e8e-11f1-a707-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</supplierDependency>
<targetDirectedRelationshipPropertyPath_>
<reflist>
<ref refid="770e6ad8-8e8e-11f1-a707-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</targetDirectedRelationshipPropertyPath_>
<text>
<val>classify sensor invalidity, watchdog reset and heater open circuit as Fault</val>
</text>
</SysML:Requirement>
<SysML:Requirement id="73d0210a-8e8e-11f1-8afa-01c58a30f183">
<clientDependency>
<reflist>
<ref refid="740c7c22-8e8e-11f1-8b54-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</clientDependency>
<externalId>
<val>REQ-SUB-SUP-022</val>
</externalId>
<name>
<val>REQ-SUB-SUP-022</val>
</name>
<owningPackage>
<ref refid="73d002fa-8e8e-11f1-96db-01c58a30f183"/>
</owningPackage>
<package>
<ref refid="73d002fa-8e8e-11f1-96db-01c58a30f183"/>
</package>
<presentation>
<reflist>
<ref refid="73efe56c-8e8e-11f1-aff1-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</presentation>
<supplierDependency>
<reflist>
<ref refid="770e6e8b-8e8e-11f1-8be3-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</supplierDependency>
<targetDirectedRelationshipPropertyPath_>
<reflist>
<ref refid="770e6e8b-8e8e-11f1-8be3-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</targetDirectedRelationshipPropertyPath_>
<text>
<val>check freshness and plausibility of every sensor once per control cycle</val>
</text>
</SysML:Requirement>
<SysML:Requirement id="73d0233b-8e8e-11f1-917f-01c58a30f183">
<clientDependency>
<reflist>
<ref refid="740e5452-8e8e-11f1-9968-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
</clientDependency>
<externalId>
<val>REQ-SUB-SUP-023</val>
</externalId>
<name>
<val>REQ-SUB-SUP-023</val>
</name>
<owningPackage>
<ref refid="73d002fa-8e8e-11f1-96db-01c58a30f183"/>
</owningPackage>
<package>
<ref refid="73d002fa-8e8e-11f1-96db-01c58a30f183"/>
</package>
<presentation>
<reflist>
<ref refid="73f1ea4b-8e8e-11f1-9b4f-01c58a30f183"/>
</reflist>
